function pubGuide(){
 const list=G.places.filter(p=>p.pubType);
 return `<a class="back" href="#">&larr; The six places</a><section class="guide-hero">${regionPhoto('west')}<div><span class="eyebrow">AROUND THE WHOLE LAKE</span><h1>The pub & beer guide</h1><p>From Irish pubs and neighbourhood bars to brewery tables and lakeside beer gardens. All ${list.length} researched listings are here, grouped by shore.</p></div></section><p>Start with the town where you will spend the evening. Finish riding before drinking, then explore on foot. A brewery name alone does not mean there is a public taproom: this directory includes places to visit, with the type of venue clearly marked.</p><div class="pub-tools"><label>Find a pub or town<input id="pub-search" type="search" placeholder="Try Bregenz, Irish, brewery..."></label><label>Type<select id="pub-type"><option value="">All types</option>${[...new Set(list.map(p=>p.pubType))].sort().map(t=>`<option>${t}</option>`).join('')}</select></label></div><p id="pub-count" role="status"></p><nav class="pub-shores" aria-label="Pub guide by shore">${G.regions.map(r=>`<a href="#pubs/${r.id}">${MEDIA.regions[r.id].label}</a>`).join('')}</nav><div id="pub-results"></div><aside class="coverage-note"><h2>About the coverage</h2><p>This is a researched directory, not a complete census of every licensed pub. It covers all six guide areas, including Radolfzell in the west and inland hop-country stops. Meersburg itself, smaller shore villages, Kreuzlingen and the western Swiss shore still need broader coverage. Listings are checked against the linked pages, not by a personal visit or a live opening-status service.</p><p>Mike's Irish Pub has a directory source only; Kolbenfresser is supported by a 2024 official tourism guide. Both are flagged for reconfirmation. Ruppaner is a brewery to know, but is not presented here as a confirmed walk-in pub. Tettnanger Krone's closed traditional restaurant is also excluded.</p><p><a href="https://www.konstanz-info.com/planen-buchen/tipps-fuer/nachtschwaermer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Konstanz nightlife directory</a> &middot; <a href="https://visitbregenz.com/en/experience-bregenz/eat-drink/nightlife-bars/bars/1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bregenz bars directory</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.radolfzell-tourismus.de/en/see-do/food-drink/bars" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Radolfzell bars directory</a></p></aside>`;
}
function updatePubs(){const q=($('#pub-search').value||'').toLowerCase();const type=$('#pub-type').value;const list=G.places.filter(p=>p.pubType&&(!type||p.pubType===type)&&[p.name,p.town,p.pubType,p.why].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(q));$('#pub-count').textContent=list.length+' places match';$('#pub-results').innerHTML=list.length?G.regions.map(r=>{const ps=list.filter(p=>p.area===r.id);return ps.length?`<section class="guide-section" id="pub-${r.id}"><h2>${r.name}</h2><p><a href="#guide/${r.id}">Open this area's full guide &rarr;</a></p><div class="cards">${ps.map(p=>card(p).replace('<div class="town">','<div class="town"><b>'+p.pubType+'</b><br>')).join('')}</div></section>`:'';}).join(''):'<p>No matches. Try another town or clear the filters.</p>';document.querySelectorAll('[data-open]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>openPlace(b.dataset.open));document.querySelectorAll('[data-save]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>toggleSave(b.dataset.save));}
function introduction(){return `<a class="back" href="#">&larr; The six places</a><article class="cycling introduction"><span class="eyebrow">GET TO KNOW THE LAKE</span><h1>Bodensee: one lake, several worlds.</h1><p class="lede">At first glance it looks like a small inland sea: a broad horizon, ferries crossing between distant towns, and mountains rising beyond the water. But Bodensee, or Lake Constance, is a freshwater lake. Understanding its shape makes the places in this guide much easier to connect.</p>${regionPhoto('lindau')}<h2>First, get your bearings</h2><p>Germany lies along most of the northern shore, Switzerland along the southern shore, and Austria at the eastern end around Bregenz. Konstanz is the useful exception to a simple north-versus-south picture: the German city sits beside Swiss Kreuzlingen at the western end of the main lake. A walk or ride there can cross a national border without leaving the built-up area.</p><p>The lake system has two principal basins. The large <strong>Obersee</strong> is the open water between Konstanz, Friedrichshafen, Lindau, Bregenz and the Swiss shore. Its long northwestern arm is the <strong>&Uuml;berlinger See</strong>, reaching towards &Uuml;berlingen and Bodman. The smaller <strong>Untersee</strong> lies west of Konstanz, with Reichenau, shallow bays and the route towards Stein am Rhein. The short Seerhein through Konstanz connects the two basins. <a href="https://www.bodensee.travel/bodensee-erleben/der-bodensee/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read about the lake's geography &rarr;</a></p><h2>A landscape shaped by water and ice</h2><p>Glaciers shaped the lake basin during the ice ages. The Rhine enters the eastern end from the Alpine region, passes through the lake system and continues west from the Untersee. This helps explain why the east feels close to the mountains while the western bays feel more enclosed. It is also a reminder that the lake is part of a much larger river landscape. <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Constance" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lake formation and Rhine geography &rarr;</a></p><p>For a visitor, the practical difference is between following the shore and turning inland. The waterfront links many towns, but the land behind it rises into hills, vineyards, orchards and hop country. A destination that looks close on a map can involve considerably more climbing than a ride beside the lake. Meersburg's upper town and the hills around Tettnang are good examples; the Pf&auml;nder above Bregenz belongs to a different kind of outing altogether.</p><h2>How the six guides fit together</h2><p><strong>Konstanz and the west</strong> suit old-town evenings and island excursions. Use Konstanz as your anchor, then treat Mainau, Reichenau and the farther western towns as individual trips.</p><p><strong>Meersburg and &Uuml;berlingen</strong> give you castle streets, promenades and the northwestern shore. Unteruhldingen sits between the two and is the stop for the pile-dwelling museum.</p><p><strong>Friedrichshafen and hop country</strong> combine a working lake town, the Zeppelin Museum and the ferry to Romanshorn. Tettnang and the breweries behind the shore add an inland dimension.</p><p><strong>Lindau</strong> is the compact island chapter: harbour, lanes, inns and several evening stops close together. <strong>Bregenz</strong>, farther east, brings the Austrian shore, swimming and the mountain backdrop. The two work well as neighbouring destinations.</p><p><strong>The Swiss shore</strong> is a chain of towns rather than one centre. Romanshorn is the ferry connection, Arbon makes a useful lakeside stop, and Rorschach adds brewery-bar possibilities. Choose one or two, rather than treating the whole shore as a single neighbourhood.</p><h2>A little history, visible as you travel</h2><p>The lake was a place to live and work long before it became a holiday destination. The pile-dwelling museum at Unteruhldingen introduces the prehistoric settlements of the lakeshore. Later, monasteries became centres of religion, learning and land management. Reichenau's surviving churches preserve evidence of the island's major medieval monastic role; it is now a UNESCO World Heritage Site. <a href="https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/974/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UNESCO: Reichenau &rarr;</a></p><p>In 1414&ndash;1418, Konstanz hosted a council that brought church and political leaders together during the division of the Western Church. Martin V was elected pope in 1417. It gives the town's old streets a significance beyond their present-day shops and taverns. <a href="https://www.konstanz.de/leben%20in%20konstanz/stadtportraet/stadtgeschichte" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City history of Konstanz &rarr;</a></p><p>Friedrichshafen tells a later story through its airship heritage. That contrast is part of the pleasure of travelling here: a medieval island town, a monastery, a brewery and a museum of modern engineering can all belong to the same lake holiday.</p><h2 id="bike-sharing">Borrow a bike, return it elsewhere?</h2><p>There are useful local bike-sharing options, but they do not form one connected network around Bodensee. <strong>Konrad in Konstanz</strong> lets you return regular bikes at another suitable station, including Mainau and Staad. <strong>Dott in Friedrichshafen</strong> offers app-based electric bicycles with permitted local return locations. <strong>RegiVelo, using Donkey Republic,</strong> serves Kreuzlingen and nearby Swiss communities. Check available bikes and the permitted destination in the app before you unlock.</p><p>For a longer ride between towns, a conventional rental may suit you better. Agree any one-way return with the rental company first. A bike that you can ride over a border is not necessarily a bike you can leave on the other side. Konrad explicitly allows riding into Switzerland, but ending the rental there is not allowed. <a href="#map/bikes">Open Bike hire on the map &rarr;</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.stadtwerke-konstanz.de/fahrrad/aktuelles/mietstation-klein-venedig/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Konrad cross-border rules</a></p><h2 id="borders">Three countries: what happens at the border?</h2><p>Germany, Austria and Switzerland are all in the Schengen area, so a day ride can cross an international border without the formalities of entering Schengen from outside. Konstanz and Kreuzlingen sit next to each other; a ride east from Lindau takes you into Austria on the way to Bregenz. However, police checks and temporary border controls can occur. Carry your valid passport, or a national identity card accepted for your nationality and journey; a driving licence is not a substitute. Travellers who require visas or residence documents should carry the relevant documents too. <a href="https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/indexamp_en.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Travel documents for your nationality</a> &middot; <a href="https://home-affairs.ec.europa.eu/policies/schengen/schengen-area/temporary-reintroduction-border-control_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Current temporary border controls</a></p><p><strong>Switzerland still has a customs border.</strong> Schengen concerns people, not duty-free shopping. If you buy goods to carry across, check the allowances for your direction of travel, particularly for alcohol, tobacco and food. Normal personal travel belongings are treated differently from purchases. <a href="https://www.bazg.admin.ch/en/travel-purchases-allowances-customs-declaration-switzerland" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Swiss customs guide</a></p><p><strong>Money and mobile data change too.</strong> Germany and Austria use euros; Switzerland uses Swiss francs. Check your mobile plan before using data in Switzerland: EU/EEA roaming rules do not automatically include it. This matters when you need an app to unlock or return a shared bike. <a href="https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/roaming-questions-answers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Roaming coverage explained</a></p><p><strong>For rental bikes:</strong> confirm cross-border permission with the operator and keep its return rules separate from your own right to cross. The same travel-document and customs considerations apply when you cross the lake by international ferry; check bicycle carriage separately.</p><h2>Think in shores and crossings</h2><p>The water joins places as well as separating them. Konstanz&ndash;Meersburg and Friedrichshafen&ndash;Romanshorn are useful ferry links, but a straight line across the map is not automatically a convenient connection. Check the terminals, bike carriage and return sailing before building a day around a crossing.</p><p>For your trip, a simple rhythm works well: choose a base with an evening you like, ride out to one worthwhile stop, and return with time to park the bikes. The local guides supply those stops; the pub guide helps you decide where you would enjoy finishing the day.</p><div class="link-list"><a class="cycle-link" href="#pubs">Explore the pub guide &rarr;</a><a class="cycle-link" href="#cycling">Plan a day by bike &rarr;</a><a class="cycle-link" href="#">Choose a place on the map &rarr;</a></div></article>`;}

render();

function mapMatches(p,key){return key==='bikes'?!!p.rentalType:key==='pubs'?!!p.pubType:key==='hotels'?p.kind==='Stay':key==='sights'?['Explore','Swim'].includes(p.kind):key==='breweries'?['johann','ruppaner','max','hopfengut','krone','korn','frohsinn'].includes(p.id):false;}
function mapFilters(){return '<div id="map-filters" class="map-filters" role="group" aria-label="Show on the map">'+[['guides','Six guides'],['bikes','Bike hire'],['pubs','Pubs & bars'],['hotels','Hotels'],['sights','Sights & visits'],['breweries','Breweries']].map(([key,label])=>'<button data-map-filter="'+key+'" aria-pressed="'+(mapCategory===key)+'">'+label+(key==='guides'?'':' <small>'+G.places.filter(p=>mapMatches(p,key)).length+'</small>')+'</button>').join('')+'</div><p class="map-filter-hint" id="map-filter-hint"></p>';}
function bindMapFilters(){document.querySelectorAll('[data-map-filter]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{mapCategory=b.dataset.mapFilter;mapArea=null;updateMapFilters();});updateMapFilters();}
function updateMapFilters(){
 const filtered=mapCategory!=='guides',places=G.places.filter(p=>mapMatches(p,mapCategory)).sort((a,b)=>mapCategory==='bikes'?Number(b.rentalType!=='Conventional rental · confirm return')-Number(a.rentalType!=='Conventional rental · confirm return'):0);
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-map-filter]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',b.dataset.mapFilter===mapCategory));
 $('.six-places').hidden=filtered;$('#map-results').hidden=!filtered;
 $('#map-filter-hint').textContent=filtered?'Places in this guide, grouped by area. Tap a count to browse; pins mark areas, not venue addresses.':'Choose a destination, or use a filter to discover places around the lake.';
 document.querySelectorAll('.lake-atlas a').forEach((a,i)=>{
  const r=G.regions[i],count=places.filter(p=>p.area===r.id).length;
  a.querySelector('text').textContent=filtered?count:i+1;
  a.setAttribute('aria-label',filtered?count+' '+(mapCategory==='bikes'?'bike hire options':mapCategory)+' around '+MEDIA.regions[r.id].label:'Open '+MEDIA.regions[r.id].label+' guide');
  a.classList.toggle('map-area-selected',filtered&&mapArea===r.id);
  a.classList.toggle('map-area-empty',filtered&&count===0);
  a.onclick=filtered?e=>{e.preventDefault();mapArea=r.id;if($('.atlas-expanded'))$('#map-enlarge').click();updateMapFilters();$('#map-results').scrollIntoView({block:'start',behavior:'smooth'});$('#map-results').focus({preventScroll:true});}:null;
 });
 if(!filtered)return;
 const shown=places.filter(p=>!mapArea||p.area===mapArea),label={bikes:'Bike hire & sharing',pubs:'Pubs & bars',hotels:'Hotels',sights:'Sights & visits',breweries:'Breweries'}[mapCategory];
 $('#map-results').innerHTML='<div class="map-result-heading"><h2>'+label+'</h2><p role="status">'+shown.length+' places '+(mapArea?'around '+escapeHTML(MEDIA.regions[mapArea].label):'around the lake')+'</p>'+(mapArea?'<button id="map-all-areas">Show all areas</button>':'')+'</div>'+(mapCategory==='bikes'?'<p class="brewery-intro">Pick up here, leave there? Try konrad in Konstanz, Dott in Friedrichshafen or RegiVelo near Kreuzlingen. These are separate local networks. Check the allowed return point before unlocking. Conventional rental options are also listed below.</p><a href="#intro/borders">Crossing borders with a rental bike &rarr;</a>':'')+(mapCategory==='breweries'?'<p class="brewery-intro">Try a brewery restaurant such as Joh. Albrecht, or make a day of Hopfengut No20: hops, brewing, a museum and a meal. Check each listing for visits and tour arrangements.</p>':'')+(shown.length?shown.map(p=>{const ph=placePhotos(p)[0];return '<button class="map-result" data-map-place="'+p.id+'">'+(ph?'<img src="'+ph.src+'" alt="" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">':'<span class="map-result-placeholder" aria-hidden="true">'+(mapCategory==='hotels'?'Stay':'Visit')+'</span>')+'<span><strong>'+escapeHTML(p.name)+'</strong><small>'+escapeHTML(p.town)+'</small>'+(p.rentalType?'<small class="rental-badge">'+escapeHTML(p.rentalType)+'</small>':'')+'<span>Photos & details &rarr;</span></span></button>';}).join(''):'<p>No '+label.toLowerCase()+' listed in this area yet. Choose another area to explore.</p>');
 if($('#map-all-areas'))$('#map-all-areas').onclick=()=>{mapArea=null;updateMapFilters();};
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-map-place]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>openPlace(b.dataset.mapPlace));
}
